.TH FS-USAGE 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fs-usage \- display filesystem capacity and check use thresholds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fs-usage
.RB [ --warn " PERCENT" ]
.RB [ --critical " PERCENT" ]
.I PATH [PATH ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the POSIX df command with -P and -k for each path and display
filesystem size, usage, available capacity and percent utilized.
Sizes are 1024-byte units. Output is tab-separated and read-only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --warn " PERCENT"
Report WARNING at or above this whole percentage.
.TP
.BI --critical " PERCENT"
Report CRITICAL at or above this whole percentage; must not be below --warn.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage.
.TP
.B --version
Show version.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Perl 5.8 or newer; a df command supporting POSIX -P and -k.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 utilization threshold reached; 2 usage error;
3 missing df, failed df or incompatible result.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR df (1),
.BR fs-report (1),
.BR quota-report (1)
